                <pb facs="0454" n="355" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg355"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.5151/334: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Philip</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-06-30T15:00:00-04:00">June 30, 1936—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>60. Referring to previous correspondence respecting our exchange difficulties
                    with Chile, I strongly advise that no further action be taken by the Department
                    until after the completion and receipt of the study of the entire question now
                    in preparation by the Commercial Attaché.</p>
                <p>The shortage of dollar and pound exchange in this market is most acute and I
                    think that no advantage would be derived from further official emphasis by us at
                    this juncture.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Philip</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
